<title>INDONESIA: Indocement says 96 net at 551.49 bln rph.</title>
<headline>Indocement says 96 net at 551.49 bln rph.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>				(in millions of rupiah unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net income			  551,489    vs    475,921</p>
<p>    Net revenues		    4,271,232    vs  3,942,267</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (rupiah)	 228    vs	  197</p>
<p>    Operating income		1,137,470    vs  1,030,167</p>
<p>    Other income		     (256,985)   vs   (366,801)</p>
<p>    Minority interest		(181,685)   vs   (151,023)</p>
<p>    Retained earnings		 619,496    vs  1,182,068</p>
<p>Note: PT Indocement Tunggal Prakarsa, a unit of the Salim Group, is Indonesia's largest cement producer. The results were audited.</p>
</text>
